ciples  of direct democracy ecology and gender  equality and inclusiveness like Laura  you know a pluralist society that that I  guess that collective that collective  memory comes back and comes back to  people quite easily and they figure out  how to live together you know in peace  and share with each other as well and I  realized that you know when we think  that certain sectarian conflicts and and  certain I guess like issues are  inevitable that it's something that we  probably need to question within  ourselves as to why we think that and so  that was I think the first step and what  I found quite quite shocking and what I  found quite shocking on the first stop  that I didn't expect to see so many  people getting along really for more  debates talks and interviews subscribe  today to the Institute of Arts and ideas  at AI TV  you
 

